.	http://purl.oclc.org/NET/cmcs/schema/:hasConfigurations		<rdf:Bag xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" > <rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/chemsys.mvm" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li><rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/SetupParams" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li></rdf:Bag>
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ORCA, B3LYP-D3BJ/ma-def2-SVP. Transition-state optimisation (OptTS) and frequencies. This calculation shows the SN2 transition state, with one imaginary mode, -341.25 cm-1, a linear Cl-C-Br arrangement (180.0 degrees), a planar CH3 group and C-Cl and C-Br distances of 2.420 and 2.473 Angstrom. Its energy is 20.8 kJ/mol above the reactant complex and 28.9 kJ/mol below Cl- plus CH3Br (computed electronic energies, no zero-point correction).
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ORCA
